WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:01.420
- It's nice to meet you, Abigail.

00:00:01.420 --> 00:00:02.320
- It's so nice to meet you.

00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:05.700
It's so funny because
I was remembering that

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:07.300
when I did Little Miss Sunshine,

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:10.670
I had to listen to headphones in a scene

00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:12.360
and I was actually listening to music

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:13.270
because Alan Arkin,

00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:14.320
there's a scene where

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:16.552
there's some language that I-

00:00:16.552 --> 00:00:17.390
- [Kelly] Oh!

00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:18.890
- cannot repeat on television.

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:23.170
And Alan was very, very,

00:00:23.170 --> 00:00:26.850
like, not comfortable
having me listen to it.

00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:28.800
So, he would always check to make sure

00:00:28.800 --> 00:00:29.750
that I had the headphones on

00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:31.230
and was actually listening to music.

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:32.810
So, I was listening to
the Breakaway album.

00:00:32.810 --> 00:00:34.160
- Are you serious?
- Yeah!

00:00:35.713 --> 00:00:36.546
- What?
- Like the whole time

00:00:36.546 --> 00:00:37.626
that you're watching that,

00:00:37.626 --> 00:00:38.500
I'm listening to-
- So...

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:39.920
- like, You Found Me.

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:40.950
- Oh my gosh!

00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:41.990
That's a deep cut.
- Yeah, mm-hmm.

00:00:41.990 --> 00:00:42.900
- Okay.
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:42.900 --> 00:00:45.610
- Wait, so technically I
was in Little Miss Sunshine.

00:00:45.610 --> 00:00:46.830
That's what I feel like-
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:00:46.830 --> 00:00:48.040
- That's what I just heard.

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:48.873
- We have to change

00:00:48.873 --> 00:00:49.706
the DVD now.
- Technically,

00:00:49.706 --> 00:00:51.030
I am a star of Little Miss Sunshine,

00:00:51.030 --> 00:00:52.520
is all I heard.
- Yes, yes.

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:53.480
Exactly.
- That's amazing!

00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:55.030
I love that they did that for you though.

00:00:55.030 --> 00:00:57.180
He was like, I'm uncomfortable
with cursing so much

00:00:57.180 --> 00:00:58.070
in front of the child.

00:00:58.070 --> 00:00:58.903
- Even at the premiere,

00:00:58.903 --> 00:01:00.406
he was like...

00:01:00.406 --> 00:01:01.590
He would sit next to me-
- He was like talking to it.

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:02.460
- and would be like-
- Ah!

00:01:02.460 --> 00:01:03.590
- to my mom and would be like,

00:01:03.590 --> 00:01:04.680
can you get her out of the theater,

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:05.700
a police light,

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:06.820
for that scene?
- Oh my gosh!

00:01:06.820 --> 00:01:08.370
- Yeah, yeah.
- That is sweet!

00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:11.350
Well, we talked about musicians, you know,

00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:12.770
that maybe inspired everybody,

00:01:12.770 --> 00:01:13.790
but what about like actors?

00:01:13.790 --> 00:01:15.620
Do you have any actors
that inspired you, Dave?

00:01:15.620 --> 00:01:16.960
- Christopher Walken.

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:18.430
- Oh my God.

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:19.263
I love this guy.

00:01:19.263 --> 00:01:20.096
- The best.

00:01:20.096 --> 00:01:20.929
Christopher Walken.
- Yeah.

00:01:20.929 --> 00:01:22.460
- I love Christopher Walken so much

00:01:22.460 --> 00:01:23.293
and there was once

00:01:23.293 --> 00:01:25.490
when we were on Saturday Night Live.

00:01:25.490 --> 00:01:27.820
And he was hosting

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:31.030
and he came up before we were about to...

00:01:31.030 --> 00:01:32.260
He was gonna introduce us, you know,

00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:33.100
as we were gonna play.

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:34.010
And he comes up and he goes,

00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:34.843
he said,

00:01:36.067 --> 00:01:39.904
"Is the accent on Foo or Fighters?"

00:01:39.904 --> 00:01:42.020
(everyone laughing)

00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:44.320
And I knew how he was gonna say it.

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:45.153
I was like,

00:01:45.153 --> 00:01:48.310
"Uh, the accent's on Fighters actually."

00:01:48.310 --> 00:01:49.877
So, he got up there and he goes,

00:01:49.877 --> 00:01:51.590
"Ladies and gentlemen,

00:01:51.590 --> 00:01:52.780
Foo Fighters."

00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:55.045
(everyone clapping)

00:01:55.045 --> 00:01:57.162
- That is so funny.

00:01:57.162 --> 00:01:58.329
- I love that.

00:01:59.650 --> 00:02:01.160
That's amazing.

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:02.130
It is funny though

00:02:02.130 --> 00:02:03.340
'cause as musicians, though,

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:04.650
we're all musicians, as well,

00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:07.270
like, I am really inspired
by actors, as well,

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:08.940
like, just as much sometimes

00:02:08.940 --> 00:02:10.750
as the musicians I grew up listening to.

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:12.090
It's just people that are creative

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:14.030
and really, like, I
don't know, inspire you.

00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:16.753
I think it's a really broad,
kind of, creative field.

